Refresh facet blocks by class, and survive a missing view instance.

A facet click fires two facet-block refreshes: one from updateFacetsView() and
one from the beforeSend() override, which piggybacks on the Views AJAX request
updateFacetsView() has just issued. Both read the block wrapper ids out of the
DOM to build their replace selectors.

Drupal appends a random --<hash> suffix to a wrapper id whenever the element is
re-rendered over AJAX, so the first response to land renames every block and the
second response is left holding selectors that match nothing. Core's insert
command then resolves an empty wrapper and calls

    Drupal.detachBehaviors(undefined, settings)

which defaults to the whole document with the unload trigger. That runs
Drupal.behaviors.ViewsAjaxView.detach over the entire page, emptying both
Drupal.views.instances and drupalSettings.views.ajaxViews. No replacement
happens, so nothing re-attaches them.

The next facet click then throws in updateFacetsView(), reading .settings off
the view instance that is no longer registered. The checkbox widget disables
every checkbox in the block before it triggers, and only a successful refresh
re-enables them, so the throw leaves the facet permanently unusable and the
checked state of the clicked facet never comes back.

Two changes:

  - facetsBlocks() addresses each block by the js-facet-block-id-<id> class the
    module already puts on it. That class survives a re-render, so the replace
    always matches and the document-wide detach never happens.

  - updateFacetsView() reads the view instance once and falls back to a normal
    page load when it is missing, so no future regression of this kind can lock
    the page up.

Related upstream, neither committed and neither covering this case directly:
https://www.drupal.org/i/3013795 (robustify how ajax finds the facet block) and
https://www.drupal.org/i/3422013 (the same id-rewrite race for a facet block
placed inside a view header).

Present in 2.0.10 and on 2.0.x HEAD. Gone in 3.0.x, which rewrote views AJAX
handling and no longer ships this file.

diff --git a/js/facets-views-ajax.js b/js/facets-views-ajax.js
--- a/js/facets-views-ajax.js
+++ b/js/facets-views-ajax.js
@@ -65,6 +65,17 @@
 
   // Helper function to update views output & Ajax facets.
   var updateFacetsView = function (href, current_dom_id, view_path) {
+    var view_instance = Drupal.views.instances['views_dom_id:' + current_dom_id];
+
+    // Bail out to a normal page load when the view instance has gone away.
+    // Drupal.facets.disableFacet() has already disabled every checkbox in the
+    // widget by this point, and only a successful refresh re-enables them, so
+    // throwing here would leave the page unusable.
+    if (!view_instance) {
+      window.location.href = href;
+      return;
+    }
+
     // Update url.
     window.historyInitiated = true;
     window.history.pushState(null, document.title, href);
@@ -74,13 +85,13 @@
     var views_arguments = Drupal.Views.parseViewArgs(href, 'search');
     var views_settings = $.extend(
         {},
-        Drupal.views.instances['views_dom_id:' + current_dom_id].settings,
+        view_instance.settings,
         views_arguments,
         views_parameters
     );
 
     // Update View.
-    var views_ajax_settings = Drupal.views.instances['views_dom_id:' + current_dom_id].element_settings;
+    var views_ajax_settings = view_instance.element_settings;
     views_ajax_settings.submit = views_settings;
     views_ajax_settings.url = view_path + '?q=' + href;
 
@@ -162,7 +173,14 @@
           return v.slice(block_id_start.length, v.length);
         }
       }).join();
-      var block_selector = '#' + $(this).attr('id');
+      // Target the block by the class facets already puts on it rather than by
+      // its id. Drupal appends a random --<hash> suffix to a block wrapper id
+      // each time the block is re-rendered over AJAX, so an id read before one
+      // refresh no longer matches after it. A selector that matches nothing
+      // makes core's insert command detach behaviours from the whole document,
+      // which empties Drupal.views.instances and breaks every later facet
+      // click.
+      var block_selector = '.js-facet-block-id-' + block_id;
       facets_blocks[block_id] = block_selector;
     });
 
